{{!
    @template local_awareness/manage/cell_validity

    The Validity cell: the scheduled window with a word for its state, or a muted sentence when
    the notice has no window at all.

    Context variables required:
    * haswindow (bool) — whether the notice is scheduled
    * window (string) — the formatted start and end, already localised
    * state (string) — expired, scheduled or current, already localised
    * permanentlabel (string) — the sentence shown when there is no window

    Example context (json):
    {
        "haswindow": true,
        "window": "1/03/26 → 31/03/26",
        "state": "Currently showing",
        "permanentlabel": "Permanent"
    }
}}
{{#haswindow}}
    <span>{{window}}</span><span class="local-awareness-subline">{{state}}</span>
{{/haswindow}}
{{^haswindow}}
    <span class="text-muted">{{permanentlabel}}</span>
{{/haswindow}}
